# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The toolbar, grown up: undo and redo (dimmed when empty-handed),
# find, renumber, and a STOP that ends a run by hand -- red only while
# something runs.  Hovering a tool names it on a tip.  Every button is
# proven by DOING: files read back, the find bar's label, the Messages
# window a stopped run leaves -- long before the 30-second bound could
# have said the same.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note a word typed, the UNDO button takes it back whole, REDO returns it
key x
key y
key z
wait 6
click 310 268
wait 8
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas xyz
click 338 268
wait 8
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas a$xyz
note hovering a tool names it: the tip's ground appears under Undo
move 310 268
wait 10
expect-pixel 316 294 ffffc8
move 500 500
wait 8
note the RENUMBER button counts the lines by tens, branches following
click 410 268
wait 10
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 10 goto 20
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 20 input a$xyz
note the stop square stands grey while nothing runs
expect-pixel 274 270 b2b2b2
note Run starts the program, which waits on INPUT for a person who is
note not going to answer -- and the square turns red, a run to stop
click 246 268
wait 20
expect-pixel 274 270 b23434
note STOP ends it BY HAND, and says so in the messages, seconds before
note the thirty-second bound would have given up on it
click 274 268
wait 30
expect-title Messages
quit
